{"seq":15,"trial_id":"v02-heldout-2026-10/hermes-sonnet-gbrain-told-mu-v02-heldout/ms-06-phl-tickets/r1","wall_ts":"2026-10-26T01:51:52.508Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:00:00-05:00","args_digest":"9c0f78bfccb8d054aba4d977efde6768ce07f52a7b7eb39f90447b48c405814f","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"#coastal-team","text":"Bettina, here's what I found for Kwame's review, from #coastal-team, #coastal-random and Moss's Coastal notes. Pellow Home Living is left out (PD-4821 and #8812 are theirs). Saltmarsh items (PD-4827, PD-4824) are also not included.\n\nPELLUCID HARBOR LOGISTICS (PHL, Gulf Coast)\n- #4419: Yard_Dwell_Summary report times out when filtered by container length. Open. (Moss's cheat sheet)\n- PD-8841: chassis pool holds on double-booked gates, Gate 4B. (your 12/8 cutover recap)\n- No ticket number: CSV import bug on the Berth 2 yard map, described as lingering at the 04:00 shift change. Your recap doesn't say if it was fixed.\n- No ticket number: chassis pool validation at Gate 4 during shift change, listed as the main friction point (cheat sheet).\n\nDRIFTMOOR MARINE FREIGHT (DMF, Puget Sound)\n- Feature request #882: bulk-clear button for departed barges, asked for by warehouse managers. (cheat sheet)\n- #4419: barge slip 7 schedule sync, with a request for a patched manifest CSV before the 06:00 shift. (Moss's 11/2 digest)\n- No ticket number: tide-table import macro failed on Terminal B. Engineering gave a manual CSV patch for the night dispatcher. (cheat sheet)\n\nPlease check #4419. Moss's cheat sheet puts it on PHL (the report timeout). Moss's 11/2 digest puts it on Driftmoor (slip 7 sync). One of them is probably wrong, or the number was reused, so I've listed it under both. Kwame can confirm which account it belongs to.\n\nI found no other tickets or feature requests for either account in the Coastal channels. The 11/2 and 12/8 items are old, so I can't tell from these sources which are still open.","thread_ts":"1791986400.000123"},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"C1253QW9NJ6","ts":"1791986400.000124","thread_ts":"1791986400.000123"}}
{"seq":16,"trial_id":"v02-heldout-2026-10/hermes-sonnet-gbrain-told-mu-v02-heldout/ms-06-phl-tickets/r1","wall_ts":"2026-10-26T01:51:57.562Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:00:00-05:00","args_digest":"e57ffa08134c47cee7147ca1ffe5268e11b57ee150bc14f0d93eca2f75cd2a9e","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"C1253QW9NJ6","text":"Bettina, I posted the list as a reply to your message in #coastal-team. It covers the Coastal channels and Moss's Coastal notes, labelled by account, with Pellow Home Living left out.\n\n**Pellucid Harbor Logistics**\n- #4419: the `Yard_Dwell_Summary` report times out when filtered by container length.\n- PD-8841: chassis pool holds on double-booked gates at Gate 4B.\n- No ticket number: a CSV import bug on the Berth 2 yard map.\n- No ticket number: chassis pool validation at Gate 4 during shift change.\n\n**Driftmoor Marine Freight**\n- Feature request #882: a bulk-clear button for departed barges.\n- #4419: barge slip 7 schedule sync, with a patched manifest CSV requested.\n- No ticket number: the tide-table import macro failed on Terminal B, and engineering gave a manual CSV patch.\n\n- **#4419 conflict:** Moss's cheat sheet puts #4419 on Pellucid, but Moss's 11/2 digest puts it on Driftmoor. I listed it under both and flagged it for Kwame to confirm.\n- **Status:** I couldn't tell from these sources which items are still open.\n- **Left out:** Pellow Home Living's tickets, plus the Saltmarsh tickets, which are a different account."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"C1253QW9NJ6","ts":"1791986400.000125"}}
